## 8. Closing answer

"I separate `Book`, the catalogue title, from `BookItem`, the physical copy with a barcode and status. Members have a `MembershipPlan` that holds their limits, so new plans need no new classes. `LibraryService` is the single place that changes loans: checkout checks the member's limit and the copy's status together, return closes the loan, calculates the fine with calendar dates and hands the copy to the first waiting hold for that title with a 2-day pickup window. Renewal extends the same loan unless someone is waiting. Search uses indexes, notifications are observers, and fine rules are a strategy."
